1
00:00:07,978 --> 00:00:10,008
(Space Rice Cake)

2
00:00:10,478 --> 00:00:12,678
(We're beginning the first business day in Seoul.)

3
00:00:13,061 --> 00:00:16,948
(The launch of the new menu item is going smoothly.)

4
00:00:17,171 --> 00:00:20,571
(The kitchen team has great teamwork.)

5
00:00:21,041 --> 00:00:22,970
(You're Table 5, right?)

6
00:00:22,971 --> 00:00:24,341
Our food didn't come out.

7
00:00:24,571 --> 00:00:27,911
(But the Seoul branch is still new to them.)

8
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:29,841
(Please give me a moment.)

9
00:00:30,041 --> 00:00:32,081
(Using a kiosk is so difficult for me.)

10
00:00:32,511 --> 00:00:36,351
(The service team starts to make mistakes.)

11
00:00:36,921 --> 00:00:39,620
(They have so much work to do.)

12
00:00:39,621 --> 00:00:42,961
(And they feel rushed.)

13
00:00:43,361 --> 00:00:47,561
(The dinner rush is already about to start.)

14
00:00:47,961 --> 00:00:50,271
(Just wait and see what our new part-timer is in for.)

15
00:00:50,601 --> 00:00:55,201
(The Earth Arcaders are exhausted and want extra hands.)

16
00:00:55,841 --> 00:01:00,181
(They're just waiting for the new recruit to join them.)

17
00:01:00,581 --> 00:01:02,340
It's 5:30pm now.

18
00:01:02,341 --> 00:01:04,380
I'll turn the sign to "open."

19
00:01:04,381 --> 00:01:05,750
- Okay.
- Yes.

20
00:01:05,751 --> 00:01:06,851
Yes, Your Majesty.

21
00:01:08,221 --> 00:01:09,981
All right. Let's go.

22
00:01:10,851 --> 00:01:14,261
(Current time, 5:30pm)

23
00:01:14,521 --> 00:01:15,861
Space Rice Cake...

24
00:01:15,961 --> 00:01:19,531
is now open for dinner!

25
00:01:19,761 --> 00:01:21,101
Okay. Let's go.

26
00:01:21,401 --> 00:01:24,201
(The members cheerfully start working in the kitchen.)

27
00:01:24,571 --> 00:01:25,871
The rice cakes are just incredible today.

28
00:01:26,231 --> 00:01:28,040
- What is that?
- They're just incredible.

29
00:01:28,041 --> 00:01:29,201
(The rice cake buns are looking extra tasty today.)

30
00:01:29,371 --> 00:01:32,071
(The dessert team also works hard to serve customers.)

31
00:01:32,311 --> 00:01:34,311
Move the less standout ones to the middle.

32
00:01:35,281 --> 00:01:39,211
(Roaming around)

33
00:01:39,551 --> 00:01:43,851
(There's no one coming toward the restaurant.)

34
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:45,721
Don't we have any customers yet?

35
00:01:46,191 --> 00:01:48,761
There's a table booked for 5:30pm, though.

36
00:01:48,991 --> 00:01:50,660
- Why haven't they come yet?
- They must be running late...

37
00:01:50,661 --> 00:01:52,561
They must be stuck in traffic.

38
00:01:52,791 --> 00:01:55,160
Why haven't they come yet? They need to arrive on time...

39
00:01:55,161 --> 00:01:56,361
so we can serve the food fresh.

40
00:01:56,731 --> 00:01:58,470
- She prepared the buns.
- I prepared them...

41
00:01:58,471 --> 00:01:59,671
so we can get two burgers out the door immediately.

42
00:01:59,931 --> 00:02:01,740
- Dinner...
- That's just the way business is.

43
00:02:01,741 --> 00:02:03,540
When you're fully prepared, no one shows up.

44
00:02:03,541 --> 00:02:05,740
- My point exactly.
- When you slack off on the prep,

45
00:02:05,741 --> 00:02:06,771
you get slammed with customers.

46
00:02:08,081 --> 00:02:10,211
You just can't predict it.

47
00:02:11,011 --> 00:02:12,350
(Just when they thought business was unpredictable...)

48
00:02:12,351 --> 00:02:13,681
That's what business is like.

49
00:02:14,351 --> 00:02:15,380
That's so true.

50
00:02:15,381 --> 00:02:18,521
(The long-awaited customers finally arrived.)

51
00:02:18,691 --> 00:02:21,420
- Welcome.
- Hello.

52
00:02:21,421 --> 00:02:22,861
Hello.

53
00:02:23,061 --> 00:02:24,961
Please come on in.

54
00:02:25,331 --> 00:02:26,391
I'm nervous.

55
00:02:26,861 --> 00:02:29,661
(The arrival of the customers freezes the chefs.)

56
00:02:29,801 --> 00:02:32,600
One Too much rice cake in a burger Beef slid in combo,

57
00:02:32,601 --> 00:02:35,070
- One tteokbokki.
- one tteokbokki...

58
00:02:35,071 --> 00:02:38,271
You can upgrade the combo drink to an ade.

59
00:02:38,411 --> 00:02:41,181
There is an additional charge of 50 cents for that.

60
00:02:41,341 --> 00:02:43,181
And you'll be served an ade instead of Coke.

61
00:02:43,281 --> 00:02:45,950
Then we'll upgrade the drink and order one ade.

62
00:02:45,951 --> 00:02:47,820
Excellent. That makes two ades in total.

63
00:02:47,821 --> 00:02:49,121
- Yes.
- We'll serve you two ades.

64
00:02:49,321 --> 00:02:51,521
Please take your time looking at the menu.

65
00:02:52,291 --> 00:02:54,220
Shrimp...

66
00:02:54,221 --> 00:02:55,561
Can I change it to an ade, please?

67
00:02:55,821 --> 00:02:56,891
Please give me a second.

68
00:02:57,461 --> 00:02:59,090
I'll upgrade your combo drink to an ade.

69
00:02:59,091 --> 00:03:00,761
Can I also get a carrot cake, please?

70
00:03:01,061 --> 00:03:02,761
The pop-up store is open as well.

71
00:03:02,801 --> 00:03:04,171
We can't sell any products, though.

72
00:03:04,431 --> 00:03:05,530
Here you go. Thank you.

73
00:03:05,531 --> 00:03:07,270
Please put this on your table.

74
00:03:07,271 --> 00:03:08,301
(She perfectly handled the order, including the table number.)

75
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:10,541
We got an order for Table One.

76
00:03:10,771 --> 00:03:12,140
The burger will go out first.

77
00:03:12,141 --> 00:03:13,240
(The kitchen gets to work right away.)

78
00:03:13,241 --> 00:03:14,311
Be careful.

79
00:03:15,111 --> 00:03:18,411
(First, she melts some butter to cook the patty.)

80
00:03:18,511 --> 00:03:20,581
(Then, she places the thick patty onto the buttered griddle.)

81
00:03:22,681 --> 00:03:26,191
(After pressing it flat with a spatula,)

82
00:03:26,451 --> 00:03:28,660
(she grills the patty until it's golden brown.)

83
00:03:28,661 --> 00:03:29,661
It's so big.

84
00:03:29,761 --> 00:03:32,191
(Meanwhile, she preps rice cakes for tteokbokki.)

85
00:03:32,561 --> 00:03:35,161
(In goes the garaetteok.)

86
00:03:35,531 --> 00:03:41,671
(She's working steadily, showing the qualities of a head chef.)

87
00:03:42,101 --> 00:03:46,371
(It's like a relay race between Seoul and Goheung.)

88
00:03:47,381 --> 00:03:50,551
There's no question about my tteokbokki.

89
00:03:52,351 --> 00:03:54,321
(There's no question about the original tteokbokki.)

90
00:03:54,451 --> 00:03:55,581
You're the problem.

91
00:03:56,681 --> 00:03:57,951
- I'm putting it on.
- That looks crazy good.

92
00:03:58,651 --> 00:04:01,420
(The dazzling steam show)

93
00:04:01,421 --> 00:04:03,221
- I like that sound.
- That's so cool.

94
00:04:03,491 --> 00:04:05,031
I really like that sound.

95
00:04:05,231 --> 00:04:06,860
I'm all about putting on a cooking show.

96
00:04:06,861 --> 00:04:08,301
(The cheese and the beef patty have finally become one.)

97
00:04:08,601 --> 00:04:10,431
(Meanwhile, our sous chef...)

98
00:04:10,771 --> 00:04:14,001
(puts the tteoksagna in the oven first.)

99
00:04:14,401 --> 00:04:19,841
(She has even finished prepping the shrimp patty.)

100
00:04:20,011 --> 00:04:22,940
I think the tteokbokki and burger can go out at the same time.

101
00:04:22,941 --> 00:04:23,981
Yes, chef.

102
00:04:24,111 --> 00:04:26,110
- Oh, we got an order...
- Okay. That's done.

103
00:04:26,111 --> 00:04:27,421
for Do you like mint? Of carrot! Cake.

104
00:04:27,921 --> 00:04:30,651
The carrot cake I'm best at making

105
00:04:31,251 --> 00:04:34,061
(She's even improvising a song as she starts making it.)

106
00:04:34,521 --> 00:04:37,561
I'll make it in advance, I'll make it in advance

107
00:04:37,661 --> 00:04:39,161
I'll make it in advance

108
00:04:39,561 --> 00:04:41,201
So that we can help each other

109
00:04:41,301 --> 00:04:43,501
(The lyrics encourage labour quite heavily.)

110
00:04:44,101 --> 00:04:49,001
(She puts a spoonful of yuzu marmalade in the cup.)

111
00:04:49,171 --> 00:04:51,470
- This will go out in five minutes.
- Okay.

112
00:04:51,471 --> 00:04:53,741
(And then she dances for a bit.)

113
00:04:53,841 --> 00:04:55,311
(The end)

114
00:04:55,741 --> 00:04:58,451
(She places gijeongtteok on top of the yuzu marmalade.)

115
00:04:58,611 --> 00:04:59,611
- And then...
- I made it.

116
00:04:59,612 --> 00:05:01,921
(Next up is the mint cream.)

117
00:05:02,351 --> 00:05:04,951
I feel like I'm both Ma Bok Rim and Ma Bok Pal.

118
00:05:05,791 --> 00:05:07,691
I feel like I'm a butcher's shop owner.

119
00:05:08,021 --> 00:05:09,061
My goodness. Gosh.

120
00:05:09,861 --> 00:05:11,361
- What's wrong?
- It burst.

121
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:12,790
Oh, my gosh.

122
00:05:12,791 --> 00:05:14,061
(The piping bag burst at the top.)

123
00:05:14,131 --> 00:05:16,501
Greed for finishing everything at once...

124
00:05:17,101 --> 00:05:18,471
always leads to a disaster like this.

125
00:05:19,571 --> 00:05:21,371
(This time, she calmly makes it one step at a time.)

126
00:05:21,641 --> 00:05:23,200
(It's finally ready.)

127
00:05:23,201 --> 00:05:24,711
(Proud of herself)

128
00:05:24,811 --> 00:05:25,840
You're so cute.

129
00:05:25,841 --> 00:05:27,481
(Chuckling)

130
00:05:27,641 --> 00:05:28,841
She was completely focused, standing next to me...

131
00:05:29,641 --> 00:05:31,650
I'm the carrot expert.

132
00:05:31,651 --> 00:05:33,951
- I'm like Torong.
- You're like Torong.

133
00:05:34,651 --> 00:05:36,451
The tteokbokki is ready.

134
00:05:36,981 --> 00:05:38,991
The burger is ready.

135
00:05:39,951 --> 00:05:42,090
We're serving the burger and tteokbokki together.

136
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:43,161
That was incredibly fast.

137
00:05:44,061 --> 00:05:45,131
I'll erase them for you.

138
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:47,460
- That was too easy.
- Exactly.

139
00:05:47,461 --> 00:05:48,631
My goodness. Exactly.

140
00:05:49,401 --> 00:05:51,501
Here's your food.

141
00:05:51,831 --> 00:05:53,470
Here's the tteoksagna. It's very hot.

142
00:05:53,471 --> 00:05:54,541
Okay.

143
00:05:54,671 --> 00:05:56,270
- We...
- This is the best day of my life.

144
00:05:56,271 --> 00:05:57,310
Sorry?

145
00:05:57,311 --> 00:05:58,841
This is the best day of my life.

146
00:05:59,041 --> 00:06:00,270
(Touched)

147
00:06:00,271 --> 00:06:01,710
She watches "Earth Arcade" every day.

148
00:06:01,711 --> 00:06:02,881
I'm deeply moved.

149
00:06:03,981 --> 00:06:05,250
It's been a long day.

150
00:06:05,251 --> 00:06:06,810
(It feels like her tiredness melts away.)

151
00:06:06,811 --> 00:06:07,851
I'm deeply moved.

152
00:06:09,121 --> 00:06:10,251
Where did you come from?

153
00:06:10,321 --> 00:06:11,321
- Yeonsinnae.
- Gupabal...

154
00:06:11,322 --> 00:06:12,620
- You came from Yeonsinnae?
- Yes.

155
00:06:12,621 --> 00:06:13,891
(The child customer came from Yeonsinnae.)

156
00:06:14,021 --> 00:06:16,191
- Please enjoy.
- Thank you.

157
00:06:18,231 --> 00:06:20,291
(Sniffing)

158
00:06:20,391 --> 00:06:21,901
(Whimpering)

159
00:06:22,201 --> 00:06:24,971
(She tries to hold back tears, but she bursts into tears.)

160
00:06:26,171 --> 00:06:27,271
- What's that noise?
- What's wrong?

161
00:06:29,671 --> 00:06:32,341
A child customer told me,

162
00:06:33,411 --> 00:06:35,711
"This is the best day of my life."

163
00:06:36,841 --> 00:06:38,311
She told me those exact words.

164
00:06:39,911 --> 00:06:41,581
(Wailing)

165
00:06:41,781 --> 00:06:44,491
- That was so touching.
- It really is.

166
00:06:45,451 --> 00:06:47,460
- "This is the best day of my life."
- That's so touching.

167
00:06:47,461 --> 00:06:48,461
Really?

168
00:06:48,561 --> 00:06:49,761
- I'm jealous.
- Does she like the food?

169
00:06:50,421 --> 00:06:51,460
She didn't tell me that...

170
00:06:51,461 --> 00:06:53,091
(Excuse me?)

171
00:06:53,491 --> 00:06:54,830
(She killed the mood instantly.)

172
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,030
- I was deeply moved.
- It's touching.

173
00:06:56,031 --> 00:06:58,031
- She just killed the mood.
- I killed...

174
00:06:58,331 --> 00:07:00,030
I mean, they paid for the food.

175
00:07:00,031 --> 00:07:01,140
(A feeling of being touched is a luxury in my kitchen.)

176
00:07:01,141 --> 00:07:02,240
She's a customer too, after all.

177
00:07:02,241 --> 00:07:03,301
(A feeling of being touched is a luxury in my kitchen.)

178
00:07:03,541 --> 00:07:07,481
(The little customers are trying the burger.)

179
00:07:08,041 --> 00:07:09,640
- The rice cake is good.
- Is it?

180
00:07:09,641 --> 00:07:11,751
(Chef Lee, she says it's good.)

181
00:07:12,251 --> 00:07:13,281
The rice cake is so tasty.

182
00:07:13,581 --> 00:07:15,651
(The food is this tasty, but...)

183
00:07:15,951 --> 00:07:19,891
(The dining area is nearly empty.)

184
00:07:20,191 --> 00:07:21,790
This is insane. Why is it so quiet?

185
00:07:21,791 --> 00:07:23,621
- Exactly. Why...
- It's like a calm before the storm.

186
00:07:23,991 --> 00:07:25,691
Why won't anyone come?

187
00:07:26,531 --> 00:07:27,801
The work is too easy today.

188
00:07:28,261 --> 00:07:29,331
Man, business is so slow.

189
00:07:29,961 --> 00:07:32,931
(But so many people checked out the place online.)

190
00:07:33,531 --> 00:07:35,600
We got 5,000 saves on CatchTable, but where is everyone?

191
00:07:35,601 --> 00:07:37,741
(Forget 5,000 people. There aren't even 5 people here.)

192
00:07:38,571 --> 00:07:40,071
Did a competitor just open up right next door?

193
00:07:40,371 --> 00:07:41,441
(Giggling)

194
00:07:42,541 --> 00:07:45,210
- Did a competitor just open up?
- That might be the case.

195
00:07:45,211 --> 00:07:47,080
Ma'am, please calm down a bit.

196
00:07:47,081 --> 00:07:49,220
We need to make money. What are you doing?

197
00:07:49,221 --> 00:07:51,021
It's not like that.

198
00:07:51,421 --> 00:07:54,090
Please calm down a bit, ma'am.

199
00:07:54,091 --> 00:07:55,521
- How can I calm down right now?
- Pardon?

200
00:07:56,061 --> 00:07:58,161
We had 5,000 people on CatchTable trying to book a table. How...

201
00:07:58,961 --> 00:08:01,131
But things are so slow. Look at all these pots I prepped.

202
00:08:01,431 --> 00:08:03,601
(She prepped so many pots.)

203
00:08:03,831 --> 00:08:06,171
- When you're fully prepared, - Exactly.

204
00:08:06,671 --> 00:08:09,170
- you don't get slammed.
- Is this normal?

205
00:08:09,171 --> 00:08:11,070
But we take reservations through CatchTable.

206
00:08:11,071 --> 00:08:13,141
I think people will come a bit later since it's Sunday evening.

207
00:08:13,411 --> 00:08:16,281
- Let me read you the new review.
- Yes, please.

208
00:08:16,481 --> 00:08:18,211
- This customer gave us five stars.
- Oh, nice.

209
00:08:19,181 --> 00:08:21,750
"The person who took our order was really cheerful."

210
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,151
"I'll never forget her."

211
00:08:23,321 --> 00:08:25,151
- That must be Eun Ji.
- There's more.

212
00:08:25,221 --> 00:08:27,290
"The lady with the twintails who waited tables..."

213
00:08:27,291 --> 00:08:29,320
"was so pretty. She could be an idol."

214
00:08:29,321 --> 00:08:31,130
- That's great.
- This customer is so sharp.

215
00:08:31,131 --> 00:08:34,031
"It was fun because the cooks were full of energy."

216
00:08:34,661 --> 00:08:37,000
- "Can you..."
- No comments about the food.

217
00:08:37,001 --> 00:08:40,101
"Can you extend it for a few more days?" That's it.

218
00:08:41,001 --> 00:08:43,100
We really are full of energy. That's all we've got.

219
00:08:43,101 --> 00:08:44,171
(Holding a grudge)

220
00:08:44,411 --> 00:08:45,870
- Are we not?
- My point exactly.

221
00:08:45,871 --> 00:08:46,941
Right.

222
00:08:47,541 --> 00:08:49,841
It's so peaceful, just like a calm before the storm.

223
00:08:50,811 --> 00:08:56,281
(A mysterious vehicle is approaching the restaurant.)

224
00:08:56,551 --> 00:08:58,991
"Could I order, please?"

225
00:09:00,221 --> 00:09:01,521
"I'd like to order, please."

226
00:09:02,591 --> 00:09:03,661
Is this it?

227
00:09:04,061 --> 00:09:06,561
(Someone arrives in front of the restaurant.)

228
00:09:08,401 --> 00:09:10,631
Goodness. I'm nervous.

229
00:09:11,871 --> 00:09:12,871
(With excitement and tension in the air...)

230
00:09:12,872 --> 00:09:13,971
Look at that. It's so cute.

231
00:09:14,941 --> 00:09:20,571
(Space Rice Cake, 2nd Earth branch)

232
00:09:23,111 --> 00:09:25,611
- Could I order, please?
- Hello... Oh, my.

233
00:09:25,951 --> 00:09:28,581
- Could I order, please?
- Hello... Oh, my.

234
00:09:29,081 --> 00:09:30,081
- Why?
- My goodness.

235
00:09:30,281 --> 00:09:32,991
- What brings you here?
- I heard about your restaurant.

236
00:09:33,421 --> 00:09:35,791
(Frozen)

237
00:09:36,391 --> 00:09:37,691
What?

238
00:09:38,591 --> 00:09:41,560
- Hello. What brings you here?
- Oh, my.

239
00:09:41,561 --> 00:09:42,930
I heard about your restaurant.

240
00:09:42,931 --> 00:09:44,171
What?

241
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:46,330
- Hey, taskmaster.
- Oh, hello.

242
00:09:46,331 --> 00:09:47,570
- Part-timer, come over here.
- Hello.

243
00:09:47,571 --> 00:09:49,970
- Hold on. You're so late.
- Come over here, part-timer.

244
00:09:49,971 --> 00:09:51,140
- What took you so long, part-timer?
- I was so surprised to see her.

245
00:09:51,141 --> 00:09:52,610
- Actually...
- Guys, she's a customer.

246
00:09:52,611 --> 00:09:54,810
- Oh, I see. I'm very sorry.
- Oh, she's a customer?

247
00:09:54,811 --> 00:09:57,410
- You're not a part-timer?
- Gosh, seriously.

248
00:09:57,411 --> 00:10:00,381
- I see. She's a customer?
- I thought she was a part-timer.

249
00:10:00,721 --> 00:10:01,880
- What should we do?
- I thought she was a part-timer.

250
00:10:01,881 --> 00:10:04,721
I'm so upset. I'm going to write a bad review online.

251
00:10:04,821 --> 00:10:06,121
I'm very sorry.

252
00:10:07,421 --> 00:10:09,320
- KARINA.
- I'll leave a bad review.

