00:18:54,581 --> 00:18:55,751
Could you put it here?

497
00:18:56,021 --> 00:18:57,280
- Gosh.
- Please be careful.

498
00:18:57,281 --> 00:18:59,491
Our child is completely stunned...

499
00:19:00,214 --> 00:19:02,254
- from seeing you.
- Get a hold of yourself.

500
00:19:02,791 --> 00:19:04,220
She's completely stunned.

501
00:19:04,221 --> 00:19:05,531
(While the part-timer is showing off her presence)

502
00:19:05,931 --> 00:19:07,330
This is the beef burger.

503
00:19:07,331 --> 00:19:09,500
(The service master keeps serving.)

504
00:19:09,501 --> 00:19:10,930
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you.

505
00:19:10,931 --> 00:19:12,401
- Thank you.
- Seriously...

506
00:19:12,791 --> 00:19:13,891
Did you order a shrimp burger?

507
00:19:14,131 --> 00:19:15,301
Yes, I ordered a shrimp burger.

508
00:19:15,871 --> 00:19:17,801
Me too. These two ordered a beef burger.

509
00:19:18,811 --> 00:19:21,341
We can cut them in half and share them.

510
00:19:21,481 --> 00:19:22,481
Sure.

511
00:19:22,941 --> 00:19:26,110
One shrimp burger and one beef burger are ready.

512
00:19:26,111 --> 00:19:27,150
- Okay.
- Okay.

513
00:19:27,151 --> 00:19:29,850
We served everything for Table Four.

514
00:19:29,851 --> 00:19:31,251
- Okay.
- We're doing very well so far.

515
00:19:31,621 --> 00:19:33,720
(A carrot cake remains, but the original order is discarded.)

516
00:19:33,721 --> 00:19:35,690
- A shrimp burger...
- It's for Table Four.

517
00:19:35,691 --> 00:19:36,891
I'll serve both of them.

518
00:19:37,091 --> 00:19:40,991
(Table 4 additional order, 1 shrimp burger combo)

519
00:19:41,191 --> 00:19:42,301
Let me give you the pickles.

520
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:45,170
Did Table 4 order 1 shrimp and 1 beef burger?

521
00:19:45,171 --> 00:19:49,041
- Yes.
- Thank you for your generous order.

522
00:19:49,401 --> 00:19:51,510
- Here's your shrimp burger.
- That's for me.

523
00:19:51,511 --> 00:19:52,670
Here you go.

524
00:19:52,671 --> 00:19:54,810
- One beef burger.
- Yes.

525
00:19:54,811 --> 00:19:56,410
Is this everything you ordered?

526
00:19:56,411 --> 00:19:58,010
We're waiting for one more shrimp burger.

527
00:19:58,011 --> 00:19:59,150
One more shrimp burger?

528
00:19:59,151 --> 00:20:01,680
One more shrimp burger and a cake.

529
00:20:01,681 --> 00:20:03,020
- That's for later.
- A carrot cake?

530
00:20:03,021 --> 00:20:04,990
- All right.
- Thank you.

531
00:20:04,991 --> 00:20:06,020
Sure.

532
00:20:06,021 --> 00:20:07,520
(She returns to the kitchen while feeling uneasy.)

533
00:20:07,521 --> 00:20:11,221
Friends, one shrimp burger is missing at Table Four.

534
00:20:11,531 --> 00:20:13,190
Why is it missing?

535
00:20:13,191 --> 00:20:14,860
(To see what went wrong, she looks at the order.)

536
00:20:14,861 --> 00:20:16,830
- Did they order two?
- One shrimp burger was served...

537
00:20:16,831 --> 00:20:18,800
to Table Four.

538
00:20:18,801 --> 00:20:21,100
We served the first one just now.

539
00:20:21,101 --> 00:20:22,640
- Take a look.
- What happened exactly?

540
00:20:22,641 --> 00:20:24,470
Table 4 ordered 2 shrimp burgers.

541
00:20:24,471 --> 00:20:26,610
- Did they order 2?
- But only 1 was served.

542
00:20:26,611 --> 00:20:27,770
Seriously?

543
00:20:27,771 --> 00:20:29,240
Table 4 ordered 1.

544
00:20:29,241 --> 00:20:30,880
- They ordered another one later.
- An extra?

545
00:20:30,881 --> 00:20:33,350
We have an extra order of shrimp burger.

546
00:20:33,351 --> 00:20:34,620
- Okay.
- Okay.

547
00:20:34,621 --> 00:20:36,151
It's for Table Four.

548
00:20:36,751 --> 00:20:38,091
I'll fry it.

549
00:20:38,551 --> 00:20:39,551
Okay.

550
00:20:39,552 --> 00:20:41,421
(There's one more thing that they forgot.)

551
00:20:41,621 --> 00:20:42,920
(The missing carrot cake wasn't even communicated.)

552
00:20:42,921 --> 00:20:45,231
Could you place some rosemary on the pomegranate ades?

553
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:49,000
(Just then, customers come out after finishing their meal.)

554
00:20:49,001 --> 00:20:51,471
KARINA, let's go and clean up together.

555
00:20:51,631 --> 00:20:54,331
(Following the service master up to the 2nd floor)

556
00:20:54,641 --> 00:20:56,470
Isn't working part-time exhausting?

557
00:20:56,471 --> 00:20:58,041
(It feels even more exhausting today.)

558
00:20:58,171 --> 00:21:02,011
Grab one of these from here.

559
00:21:02,311 --> 00:21:04,781
This is too small. Let's switch to this.

560
00:21:06,011 --> 00:21:07,110
- Right?
- Yes.

561
00:21:07,111 --> 00:21:08,921
- A bigger one is better.
- You're right.

562
00:21:09,421 --> 00:21:11,750
(Grabbing the dishcloths)

563
00:21:11,751 --> 00:21:12,890
Are you wearing an apron?

564
00:21:12,891 --> 00:21:14,691
Why don't you slip this in here like me?

565
00:21:15,191 --> 00:21:17,190
My gosh, it feels like I'm working part-time.

566
00:21:17,191 --> 00:21:20,690
(It's because you're working part-time.)

567
00:21:20,691 --> 00:21:21,730
I try to enjoy work.

568
00:21:21,731 --> 00:21:23,061
(They're off to start cleaning.)

569
00:21:23,331 --> 00:21:25,300
KARINA, everyone at this table left.

570
00:21:25,301 --> 00:21:28,301
- It looks like they enjoyed it.
- They really enjoyed the food.

571
00:21:29,001 --> 00:21:30,940
They didn't leave any food.

572
00:21:30,941 --> 00:21:31,941
It's so rewarding.

573
00:21:31,941 --> 00:21:32,941
(Feeling rewarded from seeing empty dishes)

574
00:21:32,942 --> 00:21:35,980
(Cleaning up thoroughly while thinking of next customers)

575
00:21:35,981 --> 00:21:37,581
Gosh, this is brutal.

576
00:21:37,641 --> 00:21:38,650
(A groan echoes through the hall.)

577
00:21:38,651 --> 00:21:39,911
Goodness, my back.

578
00:21:40,481 --> 00:21:41,481
My back.

579
00:21:41,482 --> 00:21:43,551
(Please let me go home.)

580
00:21:43,981 --> 00:21:46,251
- You have to go downstairs.
- Okay.

581
00:21:47,191 --> 00:21:48,621
Shall I start the dishes right away?

582
00:21:49,091 --> 00:21:50,891
I'd appreciate that, KARINA.

583
00:21:51,931 --> 00:21:54,330
Yu Jin, could you help with this?

584
00:21:54,331 --> 00:21:56,331
(The part-timer's next mission: Washing dishes)

585
00:21:56,661 --> 00:22:01,471
(Putting on the rubber gloves first)

586
00:22:01,601 --> 00:22:02,770
Are you washing the dishes?

587
00:22:02,771 --> 00:22:04,240
Yes, I'll start it now.

588
00:22:04,241 --> 00:22:05,241
I'm sorry about that.

589
00:22:05,242 --> 00:22:06,971
I'm sorry about making you do the dishes.

590
00:22:07,471 --> 00:22:08,711
Let's kiss.

591
00:22:09,941 --> 00:22:11,911
- No way.
- She likes to kiss.

592
00:22:12,481 --> 00:22:13,481
That's so harsh.

593
00:22:13,482 --> 00:22:14,651
(Getting turned down is part of her everyday life.)

594
00:22:14,821 --> 00:22:18,021
(About to properly tackle the dishes)

595
00:22:18,391 --> 00:22:21,591
(A mountain of dishes)

596
00:22:21,891 --> 00:22:23,191
I can't find the sponge.

597
00:22:24,561 --> 00:22:26,030
Has anyone seen the sponge? Here it is.

598
00:22:26,031 --> 00:22:27,991
(She found it buried in the mountain of dishes.)

599
00:22:28,261 --> 00:22:33,871
(And so began her time with the dishes.)

600
00:22:34,471 --> 00:22:38,511
(Washing the dishes in silence)

601
00:22:39,171 --> 00:22:40,270
(Laughing)

602
00:22:40,271 --> 00:22:42,010
- They didn't leave much behind.
- KARINA is...

603
00:22:42,011 --> 00:22:44,280
also working away without saying a word.

604
00:22:44,281 --> 00:22:45,880
- I know.
- She's taking it very seriously.

605
00:22:45,881 --> 00:22:47,280
KARINA, that's what happens...

606
00:22:47,281 --> 00:22:48,321
- when you're here.
- You're right.

607
00:22:48,851 --> 00:22:51,890
It's so sad. An untouched ade that almost made it out.

608
00:22:51,891 --> 00:22:52,991
(The part-timer's warmth still lingers in the ade.)

609
00:22:53,091 --> 00:22:55,191
(While the part-timer is trapped in the endless cycle of dishwashing,)

610
00:22:55,421 --> 00:23:00,791
(the next customers walk in.)

611
00:23:01,031 --> 00:23:03,931
(A frightening stream of customers comes pouring in.)

612
00:23:04,101 --> 00:23:06,730
This is our menu.

613
00:23:06,731 --> 00:23:07,871
Take your time to look at it.

614
00:23:08,371 --> 00:23:10,141
We have an order.

615
00:23:10,501 --> 00:23:12,611
We have an order.

616
00:23:13,141 --> 00:23:15,211
- Where's the tteoksagna?
- Here it is.

617
00:23:15,641 --> 00:23:17,610
Please give me one tteoksagna first.

618
00:23:17,611 --> 00:23:18,611
Okay.

619
00:23:19,211 --> 00:23:20,511
KARINA, are you okay?

620
00:23:21,521 --> 00:23:22,720
- Me?
- Yes.

621
00:23:22,721 --> 00:23:23,721
I'm okay.

622
00:23:23,722 --> 00:23:25,491
You look so lonely from the back.

623
00:23:26,821 --> 00:23:27,921
That's true.

624
00:23:28,891 --> 00:23:31,060
- Cooking can be...
- Right.

625
00:23:31,061 --> 00:23:32,061
(Her back looks especially lonely.)

626
00:23:32,062 --> 00:23:33,131
It can be lonely.

627
00:23:36,131 --> 00:23:39,571
(And here's another lonely place.)

628
00:23:39,671 --> 00:23:42,570
(Remaining order at Table 4, 1 shrimp burger combo)

629
00:23:42,571 --> 00:23:46,271
(1 mint carrot cake)

630
00:23:46,811 --> 00:23:48,111
Which one do you like the best?

631
00:23:48,981 --> 00:23:50,680
- The shrimp burger.
- Me too.

632
00:23:50,681 --> 00:23:52,580
The shrimp burger? Among these?

633
00:23:52,581 --> 00:23:53,851
(The shrimp burger tastes especially good today.)

634
00:23:54,081 --> 00:23:55,681
I want a shrimp burger too.

635
00:23:56,181 --> 00:23:57,181
(A modest wish)

636
00:23:57,182 --> 00:23:58,321
It hasn't come yet, right?

637
00:23:58,851 --> 00:24:00,551
Eun Ji, here's one shrimp burger.

638
00:24:01,421 --> 00:24:04,561
It's going to Table Five.

639
00:24:05,291 --> 00:24:07,791
(She forgot about the missing order due to so much work.)

640
00:24:10,161 --> 00:24:14,031
(Swoosh)

641
00:24:14,201 --> 00:24:17,901
The food for our perfect Romeo and Juliet has arrived.

642
00:24:18,641 --> 00:24:23,011
But Romeo and Juliet were a tragic couple, so I'll change it.

643
00:24:23,181 --> 00:24:25,610
- You're Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin.
- Oh, my.

644
00:24:25,611 --> 00:24:27,150
Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin of Yeonhui-dong.

645
00:24:27,151 --> 00:24:28,380
I'm sorry.

646
00:24:28,381 --> 00:24:29,651
I'm quite loud today.

647
00:24:29,721 --> 00:24:31,150
- Here you go.
- You're so pretty.

648
00:24:31,151 --> 00:24:32,990
Thank you.

649
00:24:32,991 --> 00:24:34,650
I have no idea either.

650
00:24:34,651 --> 00:24:35,920
(It's awkward to get angry about the missing shrimp order.)

651
00:24:35,921 --> 00:24:37,261
- I'm sorry.
- Ask her.

652
00:24:37,991 --> 00:24:39,631
Excuse me.

653
00:24:39,691 --> 00:24:41,031
We haven't gotten one shrimp burger.

654
00:24:41,161 --> 00:24:44,530
- A shrimp burger?
- Yes. And so...

655
00:24:44,531 --> 00:24:45,831
(Going back through her memory)

656
00:24:47,871 --> 00:24:50,141
(We need to get one more shrimp burger.)

657
00:24:50,201 --> 00:24:53,340
(One shrimp burger and carrot cake)

658
00:24:53,341 --> 00:24:54,341
- A carrot cake?
- Yes.

659
00:24:54,342 --> 00:24:56,010
(A promise she made with them passes by.)

660
00:24:56,011 --> 00:24:57,710
I'll go and check.

661
00:24:57,711 --> 00:24:59,211
I'm sorry about that.

662
00:24:59,551 --> 00:25:02,180
(She goes to the kitchen to share the news.)

663
00:25:02,181 --> 00:25:04,380
Everyone, that time has come for us.

664
00:25:04,381 --> 00:25:05,620
There has been a mistake.

665
00:25:05,621 --> 00:25:08,460
At Table 4, 1 shrimp burger is missing...

666
00:25:08,461 --> 00:25:10,090
and a carrot cake.

667
00:25:10,091 --> 00:25:11,691
Okay, I'll hurry and make it.

668
00:25:12,261 --> 00:25:14,360
It's not a mistake. It's almost ready.

669
00:25:14,361 --> 00:25:16,001
That time has come for us too.

670
00:25:16,031 --> 00:25:18,000
KARINA.

671
00:25:18,001 --> 00:25:20,500
Could you bring me some arugula from the pantry...

672
00:25:20,501 --> 00:25:22,771
and wash it for me?

673
00:25:23,001 --> 00:25:25,871
Seeing you together feels like the worlds are colliding.

674
00:25:26,041 --> 00:25:27,641
(Copying)

675
00:25:27,811 --> 00:25:29,680
- I'll make the shrimp burger.
- KARINA.

676
00:25:29,681 --> 00:25:31,110
Could you bring me a jar of yuzu marmalade?

677
00:25:31,111 --> 00:25:32,981
- Yusanseul? Yuzu marmalade.
- Yuzu marmalade.

678
00:25:33,881 --> 00:25:35,321
Arugula and...

679
00:25:36,451 --> 00:25:38,221
Where is it? Here it is.

680
00:25:38,691 --> 00:25:42,890
(She finds them fast with the skills used to find Black Mamba.)

681
00:25:42,891 --> 00:25:45,361
You look like someone who's been working here for a few days.

682
00:25:45,691 --> 00:25:47,260
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

683
00:25:47,261 --> 00:25:49,801
You look like someone who's been working here for four days.

684
00:25:51,031 --> 00:25:53,571
Can you give me one carrot cake?

685
00:25:56,371 --> 00:25:57,371
Gosh, the mint cream.

686
00:25:58,441 --> 00:26:00,270
(I've been flipped.)

687
00:26:00,271 --> 00:26:02,841
- I got the order wrong.
- I see.

688
00:26:03,111 --> 00:26:05,451
(For Do you like mint? Of carrot! Cake...)

689
00:26:05,551 --> 00:26:06,910
(1. Yuzu marmalade)

690
00:26:06,911 --> 00:26:08,250
(2. Gijeongtteok)

691
00:26:08,251 --> 00:26:09,651
(3. Mint cream)

692
00:26:10,321 --> 00:26:12,551
(The key is piling them in order.)

693
00:26:12,691 --> 00:26:14,550
(But what Yu Jin made)

694
00:26:14,551 --> 00:26:17,920
(Did mint go on top? Of carrot! Cake)

695
00:26:17,921 --> 00:26:19,360
Please say that it's okay.

696
00:26:19,361 --> 00:26:20,791
The beef is ready.

697
00:26:21,091 --> 00:26:23,030
- Yu Jin, be careful.
- Okay.

698
00:26:23,031 --> 00:26:25,201
- Don't get confused.
- Be careful.

699
00:26:26,101 --> 00:26:28,030
We need to serve the missing order.

700
00:26:28,031 --> 00:26:29,140
The shrimp burger is ready.

701
00:26:29,141 --> 00:26:30,801
I'll make it faster than anyone.

702
00:26:31,541 --> 00:26:34,070
I'll serve the carrot cake first.

703
00:26:34,071 --> 00:26:35,510
Okay. I'm sorry about that.

704
00:26:35,511 --> 00:26:38,711
Seven and eight for Table Four.

705
00:26:39,311 --> 00:26:41,850
- I sincerely apologize.
- It's okay.

706
00:26:41,851 --> 00:26:44,450
- There it is.
- It's very chaotic downstairs.

707
00:26:44,451 --> 00:26:48,521
- I understand.
- I sincerely apologize about that.

708
00:26:48,861 --> 00:26:50,260
We made it with extra love.

709
00:26:50,261 --> 00:26:51,860
- I apologize about that.
- Thank you.

710
00:26:51,861 --> 00:26:53,931
- Thank you.
- I'm sorry once again.

711
00:26:54,291 --> 00:26:55,961
Can I get a small plate?

712
00:26:56,161 --> 00:26:57,701
A small plate?

713
00:26:59,701 --> 00:27:01,700
Actually, small plates are at the self-service station,

714
00:27:01,701 --> 00:27:03,370
but I brought it for Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin...

715
00:27:03,371 --> 00:27:04,640
of Yeonhui-dong.

716
00:27:04,641 --> 00:27:06,641
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

717
00:27:08,441 --> 00:27:11,080
- They were available.
- Right. They were somewhere.

718
00:27:11,081 --> 00:27:12,311
(The superstar couple couldn't find what was under their noses.)

719
00:27:12,751 --> 00:27:15,120
(Meanwhile, KARINA of Yeonhui-dong)

720
00:27:15,121 --> 00:27:16,451
Mimi, do you need all of this?

721
00:27:16,721 --> 00:27:17,980
Just rinse it once...

722
00:27:17,981 --> 00:27:19,320
and give it to me fast.

723
00:27:19,321 --> 00:27:21,150
About this much?

724
00:27:21,151 --> 00:27:22,321
Okay, I got it.

725
00:27:22,621 --> 00:27:25,261
(The part-timer gets a new task.)

726
00:27:25,761 --> 00:27:28,901
(Yu Jin is making another carrot cake.)

727
00:27:29,701 --> 00:27:31,601
I got it wrong again. I must be out of my mind.

728
00:27:32,631 --> 00:27:34,471
(Current Dessert Status, Did mint go on top?)

729
00:27:36,041 --> 00:27:37,370
I must be out of my mind.

730
00:27:37,371 --> 00:27:38,841
- What's wrong with me?
- It's okay.

731
00:27:39,271 --> 00:27:40,610
Yu Jin, it's okay.

732
00:27:40,611 --> 00:27:42,640
- Thank you. Mimi.
- It's really okay.

733
00:27:42,641 --> 00:27:43,781
You're the best.

734
00:27:44,541 --> 00:27:46,151
- Yu Jin, get a grip on yourself.
- Stay strong.

735
00:27:46,581 --> 00:27:48,210
Mimi, I'm busy taking care of this.

736
00:27:48,211 --> 00:27:49,720
Could you handle the potato puffs?

737
00:27:49,721 --> 00:27:51,821
- Yes, they're in the fryer now.
- Thank you.

738
00:27:52,651 --> 00:27:54,691
The floor is slippery, so be careful.

739
00:27:54,891 --> 00:27:55,891
Okay.

740
00:27:56,761 --> 00:27:58,190
(This time, she squeezes out a lot of mint cream first.)

741
00:27:58,191 --> 00:27:59,661
The original tteokbokki is ready.

742
00:28:01,061 --> 00:28:03,701
(Sprinkling sponge cake crumbs on top)

743
00:28:04,061 --> 00:28:05,530
(Scraping the bottom very hard)

744
00:28:05,531 --> 00:28:07,131
I'll bring you more ingredients.

745
00:28:07,601 --> 00:28:08,801
Do you need sponge cake?

746
00:28:09,171 --> 00:28:11,770
- Sponge cake is hard to find.
- I'll try to find it.

747
00:28:11,771 --> 00:28:12,840
(The part-timer finds something to do on her own.)

748
00:28:12,841 --> 00:28:14,510
Tell me now if you need anything.

749
00:28:14,511 --> 00:28:15,511
Sponge cake...

750
00:28:16,081 --> 00:28:18,010
Wait, you seem a little annoyed.

751
00:28:18,011 --> 00:28:19,011
No, I'm not.

752
00:28:20,151 --> 00:28:21,651
Sponge cake crumbs...

753
00:28:23,821 --> 00:28:25,191
Crumbs should be somewhere around here.

754
00:28:26,621 --> 00:28:28,091
There's sponge cake here.

755
00:28:28,891 --> 00:28:30,920
Where are sponge cake crumbs?

756
00:28:30,921 --> 00:28:32,531
(She only sees sponge cake.)

757
00:28:32,591 --> 00:28:33,591
"Carrot."

758
00:28:33,592 --> 00:28:34,730
(For the part-timer, this place is an escape room.)

759
00:28:34,731 --> 00:28:35,731
They're not here.

760
00:28:37,561 --> 00:28:40,131
(Meanwhile, Yu Jin is finishing up the carrot cake.)

761
00:28:40,471 --> 00:28:42,440
(Carefully sticking in the shovel spoon)

762
00:28:42,441 --> 00:28:43,971
One carrot cake is ready.

763
00:28:45,071 --> 00:28:47,111
(Rushing)

764
00:28:47,371 --> 00:28:49,241
Can I take this thing?

765
00:28:50,411 --> 00:28:51,781
No one told me...

766
00:28:52,051 --> 00:28:53,281
that I had to remove the plastic.

767
00:28:54,151 --> 00:28:55,151
Are you kidding me?

768
00:28:55,152 --> 00:28:56,580
- Should I take the whole thing?
- The whole thing?

769
00:28:56,581 --> 00:28:58,490
No, take... Just take the whole thing.

770
00:28:58,491 --> 00:29:00,091
- Going back and forth is annoying.
- It's okay.

771
00:29:00,521 --> 00:29:01,521
I'm sorry.

772
00:29:01,522 --> 00:29:02,560
- You're already busy, - It's okay.

773
00:29:02,561 --> 00:29:03,621
but you got busier by coming here.

774
00:29:05,191 --> 00:29:07,060
Put the sponge cake in the sieve...

775
00:29:07,061 --> 00:29:08,461
- and crush it...
- Crush it?

776
00:29:08,631 --> 00:29:10,661
- until it becomes fine like this.
- Okay.

777
00:29:11,631 --> 00:29:14,101
Yu Jin, should I do this and put it over there?

778
00:29:14,201 --> 00:29:15,740
- Yes.
- Okay.

779
00:29:15,741 --> 00:29:16,841
(Additional task of making sponge cake crumbs)

780
00:29:17,301 --> 00:29:18,810
- Goodbye.
- Eun Ji, a carrot cake is ready.

781
00:29:18,811 --> 00:29:20,770
A carrot cake? Is it for Table Four?

782
00:29:20,771 --> 00:29:22,981
Everything for Table Four is served now.

783
00:29:23,681 --> 00:29:26,281
The beef will be ready in 20 seconds.

784
00:29:28,211 --> 00:29:29,220
Okay.

785
00:29:29,221 --> 00:29:30,820
For Table Seven...

786
00:29:30,821 --> 00:29:32,651
You're making her lonely. Why isn't anyone answering?

787
00:29:34,351 --> 00:29:36,021
I think I'm suited for this part-time job.

788
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:37,261
This is fun.

789
00:29:37,861 --> 00:29:39,090
What are you doing tomorrow?

790
00:29:39,091 --> 00:29:40,560
I have something to do tomorrow,

791
00:29:40,561 --> 00:29:41,861
but I'm thinking of coming to your company dinner.

792
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:43,960
She's realistic. She's really going to come,

793
00:29:43,961 --> 00:29:45,331
so she's talking realistically.

794
00:29:45,801 --> 00:29:47,571
- I don't say things I don't mean.
- She doesn't.

795
00:29:48,201 --> 00:29:49,201
That's scary.

796
00:29:49,471 --> 00:29:51,400
I say things just to be nice, but she never does.

797
00:29:51,401 --> 00:29:53,541
Exactly. When are you going to fix that?

798
00:29:54,371 --> 00:29:55,810
- She can't fix it.
- Right.

799
00:29:55,811 --> 00:29:57,441
In my opinion, it's a chronic condition for Young Ji.

800
00:29:57,941 --> 00:30:01,881
The carrot cake you've all been waiting for is finally here.

801
00:30:02,451 --> 00:30:04,420
I'm sorry about the long wait.

802
00:30:04,421 --> 00:30:05,851
- Don't worry.
- Okay.

803
00:30:06,021 --> 00:30:07,520
It's like rice cake.

804
00:30:07,521 --> 00:30:08,821
It tastes like donut.

805
00:30:09,621 --> 00:30:12,460
The bottom tastes like yuzu.

806
00:30:12,461 --> 00:30:13,531
- Yuzu?
- Right?

807
00:30:14,331 --> 00:30:15,601
It's very nice and refreshing.

808
00:30:17,261 --> 00:30:19,631
- Hello.
- Hello.

809
00:30:20,001 --> 00:30:21,630
We have an order.

810
00:30:21,631 --> 00:30:22,701
Okay.

811
00:30:23,241 --> 00:30:26,170
At Table 9, we have 2 ades, 1 carrot cake,

812
00:30:26,171 --> 00:30:28,310
one tteoksagna, one tteokbokki,

813
00:30:28,311 --> 00:30:30,040
1 shrimp burger, and 1 beef burger.

814
00:30:30,041 --> 00:30:31,181
- Okay.
- Okay.

815
00:30:31,711 --> 00:30:33,981
- We can do it.
- We can do it.

816
00:30:34,781 --> 00:30:36,121
You're saying that as a habit.

817
00:30:36,651 --> 00:30:38,421
If we don't do this, it's hard to stay sane.

818
00:30:41,091 --> 00:30:43,591
Young Ji, your back looks so sexy right now.

819
00:30:43,691 --> 00:30:45,360
- What?
- Your back looks sexy.

820
00:30:45,361 --> 00:30:46,561
Thank you. How about a kiss?

821
00:30:47,091 --> 00:30:48,091
Goodness.

822
00:30:48,331 --> 00:30:49,731
You're killing my appetite.

823
00:30:50,261 --> 00:30:51,261
Go away.

824
00:30:51,262 --> 00:30:52,671
(Bringing the lost appetite back)

825
00:30:53,701 --> 00:30:56,541
(2 glasses of appetizing pomegranate ade)

826
00:30:57,601 --> 00:30:59,341
Tteokbokki is ready.

827
00:30:59,911 --> 00:31:02,080
One beef burger is ready.

828
00:31:02,081 --> 00:31:03,111
Okay.

829
00:31:03,441 --> 00:31:05,850
- Can I get two ades?
- Yes, here you go.

830
00:31:05,851 --> 00:31:07,450
Gosh, part-timer.

831
00:31:07,451 --> 00:31:09,151
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

832
00:31:09,421 --> 00:31:10,450
(Thanks to the part-timer,)

833
00:31:10,451 --> 00:31:11,451
(the appetite-saving dishes are ready in no time.)

834
00:31:11,451 --> 00:31:12,451
You're a lifesaver.

835
00:31:12,452 --> 00:31:14,751
Did you order 1 original tteokbokki at Table 8?

836
00:31:14,921 --> 00:31:17,390
Did you order a shrimp burger combo at Table Seven?

837
00:31:17,391 --> 00:31:18,730
(The finished dishes are quickly served.)

838
00:31:18,731 --> 00:31:20,460
You're here as a family.

839
00:31:20,461 --> 00:31:22,061
- Yes, we are.
- Okay.

840
00:31:23,561 --> 00:31:25,330
Welcome. Hello.

841
00:31:25,331 --> 00:31:26,930
Can someone take their order?

842
00:31:26,931 --> 00:31:30,300
One burger, two tteokbokki, two cakes,

843
00:31:30,301 --> 00:31:31,441
two ades. Is that correct?

844
00:31:31,771 --> 00:31:33,810
- We have an order.
- Okay.

845
00:31:33,811 --> 00:31:36,110
At Table 10, 2 pomegranate ades,

846
00:31:36,111 --> 00:31:37,380
two carrot cakes,

847
00:31:37,381 --> 00:31:39,981
two tteokbokki, and one beef burger.

848
00:31:40,051 --> 00:31:42,021
I heard two tteokbokki.

849
00:31:42,421 --> 00:31:43,851
Two tteokbokki.

850
00:31:44,281 --> 00:31:46,351
(On the verge of being possessed by a bad spirit)

851
00:31:47,091 --> 00:31:48,551
Oh, no.

852
00:31:48,721 --> 00:31:50,561
Yeong Seok... I didn't mean him.

853
00:31:50,691 --> 00:31:52,661
Yu Jin, mashed potatoes...

854
00:31:52,931 --> 00:31:54,190
No, it's not mashed potatoes.

855
00:31:54,191 --> 00:31:55,191
What am I saying?

856
00:31:55,192 --> 00:31:57,400
- These are potato puffs.
- They're in.

857
00:31:57,401 --> 00:31:59,471
- You didn't press the timer.
- You don't need to.

858
00:31:59,731 --> 00:32:01,200
(Trying desperately to pull herself together)

859
00:32:01,201 --> 00:32:02,471
- Do it based on your feeling.
- Darn it.

860
00:32:02,741 --> 00:32:04,571
There are no buns.

861
00:32:05,001 --> 00:32:06,840
(She ends up getting possessed.)

862
00:32:06,841 --> 00:32:09,111
Calm down. It's okay.

863
00:32:09,311 --> 00:32:11,040
- What's going on?
- It's okay.

864
00:32:11,041 --> 00:32:12,151
What's going on?

865
00:32:13,711 --> 00:32:14,850
(What's going on?)

866
00:32:14,851 --> 00:32:15,921
(Scared)

867
00:32:16,081 --> 00:32:18,351
Just serve tteokbokki first. It's okay.

868
00:32:19,251 --> 00:32:22,160
Somebody, please save me.

869
00:32:22,161 --> 00:32:23,961
(One shrimp burger is made.)

870
00:32:24,291 --> 00:32:27,361
(Taking out the tteoksagna after baking it)

871
00:32:28,291 --> 00:32:30,161
One tteoksagna is ready.

872
00:32:30,901 --> 00:32:32,231
Business is booming here.

873
00:32:33,071 --> 00:32:34,470
- Isn't it booming?
- Yes.

874
00:32:34,471 --> 00:32:36,441
We have 5,000 reservations on CatchTable.

875
00:32:36,671 --> 00:32:38,001
People are just keeping an eye out.

876
00:32:38,501 --> 00:32:39,641
They're the same thing.

877
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:41,441
They keep an eye out to make reservations.

878
00:32:42,781 --> 00:32:44,010
Young Ji, stay strong.

879
00:32:44,011 --> 00:32:45,451
Stay strong.

880
00:32:46,511 --> 00:32:47,750
One original is ready.

881
00:32:47,751 --> 00:32:49,780
(The tteokbokki is complete with everyone cheering her on.)

882
00:32:49,781 --> 00:32:51,380
- My goodness.
- Do you need help?

883
00:32:51,381 --> 00:32:52,921
Could you just put this on the table?

884
00:32:53,391 --> 00:32:54,490
Yes?

885
00:32:54,491 --> 00:32:56,890
Ma'am, could we get some more pickles?

886
00:32:56,891 --> 00:32:59,030
- I'll bring you more pickles.
- Thank you.

887
00:32:59,031 --> 00:33:00,890
- Thank you. Isn't it delicious?
- Yes.

888
00:33:00,891 --> 00:33:02,501
(Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin of Yeonhui-dong like the pickle.)

889
00:33:03,331 --> 00:33:04,730
When I'm upstairs,

890
00:33:04,731 --> 00:33:08,001
people keep calling me the owner and ask for more pickles.

891
00:33:08,231 --> 00:33:09,771
They think that I'm the real owner.

892
00:33:10,041 --> 00:33:12,571
- Shall I take it to them?
- Do you mind?

893
00:33:13,041 --> 00:33:14,240
This is...

894
00:33:14,241 --> 00:33:16,111
for Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin of Yeonhui-dong.

895
00:33:16,741 --> 00:33:18,951
- I don't remember the table number.
- That's difficult.

896
00:33:19,251 --> 00:33:20,510
- Are they two people?
- Yes.

897
00:33:20,511 --> 00:33:21,850
- I'll go upstairs and ask...
- They're a couple.

898
00:33:21,851 --> 00:33:23,681
for Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin.

899
00:33:23,851 --> 00:33:25,450
Why don't you take the tteoksagna with you?

900
00:33:25,451 --> 00:33:27,050
- Take these 2.
- For Table 9?

901
00:33:27,051 --> 00:33:28,350
Table Nine and Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin.

902
00:33:28,351 --> 00:33:29,690
- Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin.
- Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin...

903
00:33:29,691 --> 00:33:30,891
- of Yeonhui-dong.
- Okay.

904
00:33:31,621 --> 00:33:35,131
(She's going to meet them now.)

905
00:33:37,001 --> 00:33:38,100
My goodness.

906
00:33:38,101 --> 00:33:39,301
Hello.

907
00:33:39,771 --> 00:33:41,430
- Hello.
- Here's your tteoksagna.

908
00:33:41,431 --> 00:33:42,571
Why are you here?

909
00:33:43,201 --> 00:33:44,241
I'm not sure.

910
00:33:44,271 --> 00:33:45,271
Gosh, it's hot.

911
00:33:45,272 --> 00:33:46,870
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you.

912
00:33:46,871 --> 00:33:48,110
Which one of you is...

913
00:33:48,111 --> 00:33:49,981
Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin of Yeonhui-dong?

914
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:51,111
(What?)

915
00:33:52,081 --> 00:33:53,310
(At the top of her lungs)

916
00:33:53,311 --> 00:33:54,511
(Which one of you is Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin of Yeonhui-dong?)

917
00:33:57,421 --> 00:33:59,391
Is it you?

918
00:34:00,551 --> 00:34:02,291
- I don't think it's me.
- It's not you?

919
00:34:02,521 --> 00:34:03,560
Are you really not?

920
00:34:03,561 --> 00:34:05,261
- I asked for more pickle.
- Really?

921
00:34:05,631 --> 00:34:06,991
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

922
00:34:07,191 --> 00:34:08,390
- You look great together.
- Thank you.

923
00:34:08,391 --> 00:34:10,031
(You look great together.)

924
00:34:10,431 --> 00:34:13,631
(KARINA of Yeonhui-dong completed her mission with a hearty laugh.)

925
00:34:13,731 --> 00:34:15,201
(Groaning)

926
00:34:15,601 --> 00:34:16,801
We shouldn't have asked for more.

927
00:34:18,471 --> 00:34:19,471
It feels hot.

928
00:34:20,311 --> 00:34:23,781
(Hyun Bin of Yeonhui-dong gets hot easily.)

929
00:34:25,141 --> 00:34:26,781
Did you find Hyun Bin and Son Ye Jin?

930
00:34:27,211 --> 00:34:28,250
They asked for more pickle,

931
00:34:28,251 --> 00:34:29,281
but they said that they weren't Hyun Bin or Son Ye Jin.

932
00:34:29,651 --> 00:34:30,780
(Satisfied)

933
00:34:30,781 --> 00:34:33,551
- Did you ask that?
- Yes. I didn't know who they were.

934
00:34:34,391 --> 00:34:36,961
(While the part-timer was doing all the work, the head chef...)

935
00:34:37,691 --> 00:34:40,461
(She melted cheese on the patties.)

936
00:34:40,891 --> 00:34:41,931
Director.

937
00:34:42,731 --> 00:34:43,960
Have you ever seen a woman...

938
00:34:43,961 --> 00:34:45,061
making tteokbokki while making burgers?

939
00:34:45,301 --> 00:34:47,201
(It's a rare sight.)

940
00:34:47,431 --> 00:34:48,470
Right?

941
00:34:48,471 --> 00:34:50,971
(This rare woman's tteokbokki is almost ready.)

942
00:34:51,201 --> 00:34:53,941
(The well-cooked beef patties are taken off the grill.)

943
00:34:54,611 --> 00:34:55,811
The rice cakes are ready.

944
00:34:56,181 --> 00:34:57,710
No, I mean the burgers.

945
00:34:57,711 --> 00:34:58,781
Burgers.

946
00:34:58,881 --> 00:35:01,550
(A hearty laugh that's rare)

947
00:35:01,551 --> 00:35:02,581
Goodness.

948
00:35:02,951 --> 00:35:05,250
Burgers are ready. Two of them are ready.

949
00:35:05,251 --> 00:35:06,591
(Two rice cake burgers are ready.)

950
00:35:06,951 --> 00:35:08,490
Young Ji, is the original tteokbokki...

951
00:35:08,491 --> 00:35:09,760
ready yet?

952
00:35:09,761 --> 00:35:10,791
In one minute.

953
00:35:11,161 --> 00:35:12,630
It'd be perfect to serve them together.

954
00:35:12,631 --> 00:35:13,830
One minute and 20 seconds.

955
00:35:13,831 --> 00:35:16,201
- You added 20 seconds.
- Both at the same time.

956
00:35:16,861 --> 00:35:19,070
I want to feel the thrill of serving two at the same time.

957
00:35:19,071 --> 00:35:20,430
- I'll make you feel it.
- We need to serve one beef...

958
00:35:20,431 --> 00:35:21,431
I'll give you that catharsis.

959
00:35:21,432 --> 00:35:23,001
One beef burger needs to go out.

960
00:35:23,171 --> 00:35:24,200
I'll give it to you in three minutes.

961
00:35:24,201 --> 00:35:25,840
Three minutes? Why is the time increasing?

962
00:35:25,841 --> 00:35:27,040
In four minutes.

963
00:35:27,041 --> 00:35:28,171
(Screaming)

964
00:35:28,411 --> 00:35:31,010
(Total chaos)

965
00:35:31,011 --> 00:35:32,081
Do something.

966
00:35:33,551 --> 00:35:37,021
(New customers enter.)

967
00:35:37,121 --> 00:35:38,751
(However...)

968
00:35:39,051 --> 00:35:41,991
(The current situation at Space Rice Cake's hall)

969
00:35:42,861 --> 00:35:45,421
(In the secondary hall)

970
00:35:45,761 --> 00:35:47,760
(And in the main hall)

971
00:35:47,761 --> 00:35:50,961
(The only seats left are tables that haven't been cleared.)

972
00:35:51,131 --> 00:35:53,200
Hello. I'll take your order.

973
00:35:53,201 --> 00:35:54,300
(Unaware of the situation, the servers keep taking orders.)

974
00:35:54,301 --> 00:35:56,701
- One shrimp burger.
- One tteokbokki.

975
00:35:57,571 --> 00:35:59,870
Here you go. Thank you.

976
00:35:59,871 --> 00:36:02,380
(She sends the customers to the 2nd floor.)

977
00:36:02,381 --> 00:36:03,481
Is this it?

978
00:36:03,981 --> 00:36:05,041
Where?

979
00:36:05,951 --> 00:36:07,010
Where should we sit?

980
00:36:07,011 --> 00:36:08,450
- Where shall we sit?
- No.

981
00:36:08,451 --> 00:36:09,680
- No.
- The seats...

982
00:36:09,681 --> 00:36:12,351
(The floor manager doesn't notice the situation.)

983
00:36:14,251 --> 00:36:16,261
They have to clear the table.

984
00:36:16,791 --> 00:36:19,291
(Wandering around endlessly)

985
00:36:19,631 --> 00:36:20,890
(Thankfully, they find a server.)

986
00:36:20,891 --> 00:36:22,130
Could we...

987
00:36:22,131 --> 00:36:23,431
Where should we sit?

988
00:36:23,661 --> 00:36:24,861
Where should you sit?

989
00:36:25,401 --> 00:36:26,631
On top of my knees.

990
00:36:27,631 --> 00:36:29,370
- Please wait.
- Thank you.

991
00:36:29,371 --> 00:36:30,740
I'll clear the table. I'm sorry.

992
00:36:30,741 --> 00:36:31,771
It's okay.

993
00:36:32,001 --> 00:36:34,370
I'm very sorry. You made a reservation on CatchTable,

994
00:36:34,371 --> 00:36:36,041
and we neglected to clear the tables.

995
00:36:36,881 --> 00:36:38,640
This is the worst restaurant ever.

996
00:36:38,641 --> 00:36:39,881
(A self-deprecating assessment)

997
00:36:41,081 --> 00:36:42,381
(Glancing)

998
00:36:43,321 --> 00:36:45,180
I'm very busy, but I'll still fix my apron.

999
00:36:45,181 --> 00:36:46,790
Sure. Take your time.

1000
00:36:46,791 --> 00:36:47,820
(Rummaging)

1001
00:36:47,821 --> 00:36:48,821
Goodness.

1002
00:36:48,822 --> 00:36:49,891
(Running away)

1003
00:36:50,791 --> 00:36:52,061
It's an apron show.

1004
00:36:52,761 --> 00:36:53,761
It's no ordinary task.

1005
00:36:53,762 --> 00:36:56,031
(A special show performed out of sheer guilt)

1006
00:36:57,431 --> 00:36:59,031
I love you, customers.

1007
00:36:59,701 --> 00:37:00,731
I'm sorry about that.

1008
00:37:00,931 --> 00:37:02,601
- You're Table One.
- That's right.

1009
00:37:03,201 --> 00:37:04,600
- KARINA, we have to clean up.
- Okay.

1010
00:37:04,601 --> 00:37:05,670
Clean the tables in the room.

1011
00:37:05,671 --> 00:37:06,940
(Cleaning the remaining tables with the part-timer)

1012
00:37:06,941 --> 00:37:07,971
- Excuse me.
- Eun Ji, are there customers...

1013
00:37:08,511 --> 00:37:09,541
Gosh, hello.

1014
00:37:11,081 --> 00:37:13,650
- It's a baby.
- I see. I'm sorry for creating...

1015
00:37:13,651 --> 00:37:16,981
a bad environment while you're eating.

1016
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:20,051
- I sincerely apologize once again.
- I'm sorry.

1017
00:37:20,351 --> 00:37:22,820
Don't worry. The work must be very hard.

1018
00:37:22,821 --> 00:37:23,860
- It's okay.
- It's all right.

1019
00:37:23,861 --> 00:37:25,891
I can tell how tired you are on your face.

1020
00:37:27,131 --> 00:37:28,131
Are you saying that I have grease...

1021
00:37:29,501 --> 00:37:31,501
