1112
00:41:07,351 --> 00:41:08,611
- Mimi.
- Yes?

1113
00:41:09,051 --> 00:41:10,621
I'll grill it this time.

1114
00:41:10,921 --> 00:41:12,820
No.

1115
00:41:12,821 --> 00:41:14,691
Yu Jin... I mean, Young...

1116
00:41:15,891 --> 00:41:19,661
(Cutting the rice cakes so perfectly that it leaves you speechless)

1117
00:41:20,291 --> 00:41:21,691
Mimi, we're out of shrimp again.

1118
00:41:22,031 --> 00:41:25,061
We're out of shrimp again? Here's some more. Come here.

1119
00:41:25,261 --> 00:41:26,330
(Restocking the fried food in between)

1120
00:41:26,331 --> 00:41:28,230
- Be careful.
- I'll do this first.

1121
00:41:28,231 --> 00:41:29,301
(Restocking the fried food in between)

1122
00:41:30,201 --> 00:41:34,011
(Even 10 pairs of hands wouldn't be enough right now.)

1123
00:41:34,511 --> 00:41:35,810
- KARINA.
- Yes?

1124
00:41:35,811 --> 00:41:39,040
Could you bring me some potato puffs from the pantry?

1125
00:41:39,041 --> 00:41:41,280
- Potato?
- Potato.

1126
00:41:41,281 --> 00:41:44,081
They're called potato puffs. They're like hash browns.

1127
00:41:45,051 --> 00:41:46,121
The pronunciation must be unfamiliar.

1128
00:41:46,991 --> 00:41:50,961
(However, the pantry is no longer unfamiliar to her.)

1129
00:41:51,561 --> 00:41:53,560
(She brings potato puffs for Mimi.)

1130
00:41:53,561 --> 00:41:55,900
Thank you so much. Goodness.

1131
00:41:55,901 --> 00:41:56,901
The sponge cake is down here.

1132
00:41:57,361 --> 00:41:59,400
Thank you.

1133
00:41:59,401 --> 00:42:00,471
