- I think...

1744
01:02:44,341 --> 01:02:46,710
I rolled it vertically first.

1745
01:02:46,711 --> 01:02:48,410
Then I flipped it and rolled it horizontally.

1746
01:02:48,411 --> 01:02:49,911
Then I made the shape.

1747
01:02:50,181 --> 01:02:52,121
(It's easier said than done.)

1748
01:02:52,321 --> 01:02:55,091
(The head chef is trying to flip it.)

1749
01:02:55,321 --> 01:02:57,760
(But the dough won't come off the pan.)

1750
01:02:57,761 --> 01:02:59,591
Push it forward and flip it.

1751
01:02:59,691 --> 01:03:01,331
(Her second attempt)

1752
01:03:02,361 --> 01:03:04,330
(She finally pulls it off!)

1753
01:03:04,331 --> 01:03:05,900
- Where do I put it?
- Nice.

1754
01:03:05,901 --> 01:03:07,301
(Where do I put it?)

1755
01:03:07,901 --> 01:03:09,400
- Place another one, please.
- You do look...

1756
01:03:09,401 --> 01:03:11,601
- like a real Italian chef.
- Yes.

1757
01:03:12,541 --> 01:03:14,741
- No.
- The measuring queen.

1758
01:03:14,941 --> 01:03:16,770
(After mixing the spicy-looking sauce well,)

1759
01:03:16,771 --> 01:03:18,611
How does this look, Young Ji?

1760
01:03:18,741 --> 01:03:21,481
(it's time for a mid-way check.)

1761
01:03:21,811 --> 01:03:23,110
- It's perfect.
- Is it?

1762
01:03:23,111 --> 01:03:25,021
Try it, Yu Jin.

1763
01:03:25,351 --> 01:03:27,021
It's not spicy at all.

1764
01:03:27,291 --> 01:03:28,691
Isn't it a mushroom pizza?

1765
01:03:29,151 --> 01:03:30,691
Shall we bake it?

1766
01:03:31,191 --> 01:03:33,361
- Bake it.
- Bake it, please.

1767
01:03:33,561 --> 01:03:36,631
(They bake it nice and hot.)

1768
01:03:36,761 --> 01:03:38,230
- I want lots of cheese.
- Yes.

1769
01:03:38,231 --> 01:03:39,930
- The bottom is...
- It's fine.

1770
01:03:39,931 --> 01:03:41,701
(They sprinkle it with cheese to finish.)

1771
01:03:42,171 --> 01:03:43,630
Please give it a try.

1772
01:03:43,631 --> 01:03:44,701
(The ghost pepper pizza is ready.)

1773
01:03:44,741 --> 01:03:46,870
Dip it in honey. We need to serve it with honey, everyone.

1774
01:03:46,871 --> 01:03:47,871
- Yes.
- That's right.

1775
01:03:47,872 --> 01:03:51,811
(Trying it)

1776
01:03:53,481 --> 01:03:54,581
How is it?

1777
01:03:56,681 --> 01:03:58,020
- Is it good?
- She likes it.

1778
01:03:58,021 --> 01:03:59,181
- Is it good, Eun Ji?
- This is it.

1779
01:03:59,381 --> 01:04:00,480
Ghost pepper tastes good, doesn't it?

1780
01:04:00,481 --> 01:04:02,121
The ghost pepper tastes incredible.

1781
01:04:02,221 --> 01:04:04,220
(The head chef tries it too.)

1782
01:04:04,221 --> 01:04:05,260
How is it?

1783
01:04:05,261 --> 01:04:06,760
(The sous chef takes a bite too.)

1784
01:04:06,761 --> 01:04:07,831
I'll take it.

1785
01:04:08,931 --> 01:04:09,991
Is it good?

1786
01:04:10,431 --> 01:04:12,061
I told you it was good.

1787
01:04:13,231 --> 01:04:14,700
It tastes like the ghost pepper I know.

1788
01:04:14,701 --> 01:04:16,330
(Everyone loves how deliciously spicy it is.)

1789
01:04:16,331 --> 01:04:18,400
- It's tasty.
- Ghost pepper's better than Buldak.

1790
01:04:18,401 --> 01:04:19,771
Dipping it in honey...

1791
01:04:20,571 --> 01:04:22,340
- makes it even better.
- It tastes better.

1792
01:04:22,341 --> 01:04:24,380
Let's do a limited quantity of ten pizzas.

1793
01:04:24,381 --> 01:04:26,081
- Let's do 10.
- Let's make 10.

1794
01:04:26,541 --> 01:04:27,751
Great idea.

1795
01:04:27,981 --> 01:04:32,151
I'm going to make a Goheung sea margarita.

1796
01:04:32,581 --> 01:04:34,151
(Last night)

1797
01:04:34,421 --> 01:04:35,720
- Then...
- Should we change it?

1798
01:04:35,721 --> 01:04:37,050
should we add a refreshing drink...

1799
01:04:37,051 --> 01:04:39,120
- to the pizza?
- Sounds good.

1800
01:04:39,121 --> 01:04:41,560
Should I make it with a shaker?

1801
01:04:41,561 --> 01:04:43,691
- A non-alcoholic one.
- Sounds great.

1802
01:04:43,791 --> 01:04:47,130
I'll try making some stuff tomorrow.

1803
01:04:47,131 --> 01:04:48,201
Try them tomorrow.

1804
01:04:48,271 --> 01:04:51,071
(It's clear and blue like the sea of Goheung.)

1805
01:04:51,471 --> 01:04:54,111
(It's sweet, sour, and refreshing.)

1806
01:04:54,241 --> 01:04:56,911
(New drink: Non-alcoholic Goheung sea margarita)

1807
01:04:57,111 --> 01:04:58,180
(Setting the cocktail shaker)

1808
01:04:58,181 --> 01:04:59,311
I've never used it before.

1809
01:04:59,541 --> 01:05:01,551
Two tablespoons of peach juice.

1810
01:05:03,181 --> 01:05:04,850
I love grapefruit juice.

1811
01:05:04,851 --> 01:05:05,881
(Grapefruit juice)

1812
01:05:06,081 --> 01:05:07,991
I'm going to recreate the sea of Goheung.

1813
01:05:08,191 --> 01:05:09,421
Nice.

1814
01:05:09,751 --> 01:05:11,590
(Sparkling water)

1815
01:05:11,591 --> 01:05:13,091
Two tablespoons of sparkling water.

1816
01:05:13,421 --> 01:05:15,891
(Ice)

1817
01:05:15,991 --> 01:05:17,301
- Yu Jin.
- Yes?

1818
01:05:17,401 --> 01:05:18,830
Do you want me to cheer you up?

1819
01:05:18,831 --> 01:05:20,160
Yes, please.

1820
01:05:20,161 --> 01:05:21,301
Hold on.

1821
01:05:23,931 --> 01:05:25,840
- You and I - And I

1822
01:05:25,841 --> 01:05:27,610
- It's more than "Like"
- It's more than "Like"

1823
01:05:27,611 --> 01:05:30,981
(L, O, and yes)

1824
01:05:31,181 --> 01:05:34,011
(You and I, it's more than "Like")

1825
01:05:34,151 --> 01:05:35,711
(Super excited)

1826
01:05:35,981 --> 01:05:38,581
(A tribute to Yu Jin who's tired)

1827
01:05:38,651 --> 01:05:40,921
- You look like a happy seal.
- Thanks.

1828
01:05:41,351 --> 01:05:44,490
(Playing the next song, riding the momentum)

1829
01:05:44,491 --> 01:05:46,920
(This one is for the second eldest sister.)

1830
01:05:46,921 --> 01:05:48,591
Mimi, look at me while working on it.

1831
01:05:49,661 --> 01:05:51,061
(My heart fluttered a little)

1832
01:05:51,401 --> 01:05:52,700
No! Goodness.

1833
01:05:52,701 --> 01:05:53,831
Gosh. I'm sorry.

1834
01:05:54,131 --> 01:05:57,131
(Starting the next song with the same spirit)

1835
01:05:57,341 --> 01:05:59,641
(This time, it's a performance for the second sister.)

1836
01:05:59,801 --> 01:06:01,311
Watch as you're doing that, Mimi.

1837
01:06:02,411 --> 01:06:03,941
I was a little flustered

1838
01:06:05,011 --> 01:06:06,611
I'm sorry.

1839
01:06:06,881 --> 01:06:07,910
(The show was cut short.)

1840
01:06:07,911 --> 01:06:09,451
- I'm sorry.
- Goodness.

1841
01:06:09,751 --> 01:06:10,751
Goodness.

1842
01:06:11,151 --> 01:06:12,781
- We've become happy.
- Goodness.

1843
01:06:13,151 --> 01:06:14,320
It was like the Waterbomb Festival.

1844
01:06:14,321 --> 01:06:15,450
- It was nice.
- I'm not used to...

1845
01:06:15,451 --> 01:06:17,721
I'll do it. Your hands are meant to eat food.

1846
01:06:17,961 --> 01:06:19,160
(I spilled it a little.)

1847
01:06:19,161 --> 01:06:20,190
This is funny.

1848
01:06:20,191 --> 01:06:23,231
They do things like this at cocktail bars.

1849
01:06:23,361 --> 01:06:26,461
Like this. They rim the glass with lemon juice...

1850
01:06:26,601 --> 01:06:29,801
and sugar.

1851
01:06:30,271 --> 01:06:32,140
We can add a garnish.

1852
01:06:32,141 --> 01:06:33,201
(Perching lemon on the edge of the glass)

1853
01:06:33,401 --> 01:06:35,411
(It's time to pour the cocktail from the shaker.)

1854
01:06:35,611 --> 01:06:37,340
Goodness. That looks pretty.

1855
01:06:37,341 --> 01:06:38,640
- It looks so pretty.
- Does it look okay?

1856
01:06:38,641 --> 01:06:40,010
- It feels like I'm at a resort.
- Does it look okay?

1857
01:06:40,011 --> 01:06:42,451
- It looks really pretty.
- Does it look like a pretty sea?

1858
01:06:42,881 --> 01:06:44,080
- Totally.
- It looks like a pretty sea.

1859
01:06:44,081 --> 01:06:47,491
(The head chef tastes first.)

1860
01:06:48,051 --> 01:06:49,090
(She approves.)

1861
01:06:49,091 --> 01:06:50,151
Is it okay?

1862
01:06:50,821 --> 01:06:53,421
(The dessert master also takes a sip.)

1863
01:06:53,621 --> 01:06:55,530
You definitely are an all-rounder.

1864
01:06:55,531 --> 01:06:57,831
It felt like a real evaluation. It was like "Culinary Class Wars."

1865
01:06:58,001 --> 01:06:59,900
Thank you for the compliment.

1866
01:06:59,901 --> 01:07:00,901
(A new menu item is ready!)

1867
01:07:00,902 --> 01:07:03,100
- Let's eat something.
- Okay.

1868
01:07:03,101 --> 01:07:04,700
Let's eat quickly.

1869
01:07:04,701 --> 01:07:05,941
- Have some.
- Thank you for the meal.

1870
01:07:06,501 --> 01:07:07,641
Enjoy.

1871
01:07:07,771 --> 01:07:08,810
- Is it ready?
- Enjoy.

1872
01:07:08,811 --> 01:07:10,241
(Eating)

1873
01:07:10,511 --> 01:07:11,840
It's like eating ramyeon...

1874
01:07:11,841 --> 01:07:13,141
- at a ski resort.
- Right.

1875
01:07:13,381 --> 01:07:16,580
I think we should just assume...

1876
01:07:16,581 --> 01:07:19,281
it'll be a bit chaotic in the morning.

1877
01:07:19,721 --> 01:07:21,191
The kitchen is always a little chaotic.

1878
01:07:21,951 --> 01:07:23,551
Think about what we have to prepare.

1879
01:07:24,021 --> 01:07:26,691
(She's talking about work already.)

1880
01:07:27,061 --> 01:07:29,130
- Eun Ji, the pomegranate ade...
- Yes, chef.

1881
01:07:29,131 --> 01:07:30,860
You're only making the pomegranate ade and margarita, right?

1882
01:07:30,861 --> 01:07:32,801
Yu Jin...

1883
01:07:32,901 --> 01:07:34,871
- is on the carrot cake...
- I'm on pomegranate ade...

1884
01:07:35,201 --> 01:07:36,701
- and carrot cake.
- Yes.

1885
01:07:36,801 --> 01:07:39,541
- Mimi will prepare pizza here.
- Yes.

1886
01:07:39,701 --> 01:07:41,140
I just need to make pizza and fritters.

1887
01:07:41,141 --> 01:07:44,541
I'll make tteokbokki, burgers, and fritters.

1888
01:07:44,741 --> 01:07:47,950
Please take good care of the hall with our precious customers.

1889
01:07:47,951 --> 01:07:49,981
- Our guardian angels.
- Yes, chef.

1890
01:07:50,411 --> 01:07:52,650
But things don't go as expected in restaurants.

1891
01:07:52,651 --> 01:07:55,521
- Right. Nothing goes as planned.
- Let's prepare as much as we can.

1892
01:07:55,891 --> 01:07:56,891
- Yes.
- Right.

1893
01:07:56,892 --> 01:07:58,321
(20 minutes before opening)

1894
01:07:58,591 --> 01:08:00,521
- I feel like throwing up.
- Right.

1895
01:08:01,231 --> 01:08:02,791
We have to hurry.

1896
01:08:03,791 --> 01:08:05,801
The torture began again.

1897
01:08:06,061 --> 01:08:08,330
(They have no choice but to do it.)

1898
01:08:08,331 --> 01:08:09,431
Right.

1899
01:08:10,131 --> 01:08:11,240
We can put it down.

1900
01:08:11,241 --> 01:08:13,171
(She sets the carrot cakes for faster serving.)

1901
01:08:13,341 --> 01:08:14,370
(They're ready to open!)

1902
01:08:14,371 --> 01:08:16,571
I'm baking the bread. I'm almost done.

1903
01:08:17,211 --> 01:08:19,340
I think we need a new part-timer today.

1904
01:08:19,341 --> 01:08:20,881
The part-timer needs to come quickly.

1905
01:08:21,481 --> 01:08:23,581
We're going to make...

1906
01:08:23,881 --> 01:08:25,681
good use of the part-timer.

1907
01:08:26,021 --> 01:08:28,451
(Current time, 11:30am)

1908
01:08:28,921 --> 01:08:31,391
(Enjoying the last moment of calm before opening)

1909
01:08:31,761 --> 01:08:35,161
Opening the sign

1910
01:08:35,661 --> 01:08:37,861
We're open. Welcome!

1911
01:08:38,431 --> 01:08:39,800
Thank you for visiting.

1912
01:08:39,801 --> 01:08:41,001
(They're open for lunch now.)

1913
01:08:41,301 --> 01:08:42,470
Thank you for your service.

1914
01:08:42,471 --> 01:08:44,271
(Good luck today.)

1915
01:08:44,771 --> 01:08:46,871
(Starting Day Two with a clean workspace)

1916
01:08:47,341 --> 01:08:48,711
We'll have pizza here.

1917
01:08:49,211 --> 01:08:51,541
- This will be the burger tray.
- Okay.

1918
01:08:52,541 --> 01:08:55,410
(The first customers arrive.)

1919
01:08:55,411 --> 01:08:57,180
We love you to the space.

1920
01:08:57,181 --> 01:08:59,381
Welcome to Space Rice Cake.

1921
01:08:59,481 --> 01:09:01,491
I'm glad you came today.

1922
01:09:01,791 --> 01:09:02,891
You have a new pizza item.

1923
01:09:04,461 --> 01:09:06,561
- We studied in advance.
- Thank you so much.

1924
01:09:06,691 --> 01:09:09,631
Please take your time to order.

1925
01:09:10,091 --> 01:09:12,331
(The kitchen is nervous even before the first order.)

1926
01:09:12,761 --> 01:09:14,301
Please head upstairs.

1927
01:09:14,631 --> 01:09:16,631
Please help yourselves to dishes and utensils. Take this.

1928
01:09:16,771 --> 01:09:19,170
One beef burger, one shrimp burger, one original tteokbokki,

1929
01:09:19,171 --> 01:09:22,710
one pizza, one carrot cake, one margarita, and one soda.

1930
01:09:22,711 --> 01:09:24,040
(The first customers order the entire menu.)

1931
01:09:24,041 --> 01:09:25,381
That's Table One.

1932
01:09:25,781 --> 01:09:27,211
Margarita, as in the pizza?

1933
01:09:27,711 --> 01:09:28,711
It's the pizza...

1934
01:09:28,712 --> 01:09:30,351
- Margarita isn't pizza.
- Okay.

1935
01:09:30,921 --> 01:09:33,121
(I'm ghost pepper pizza.)

1936
01:09:33,551 --> 01:09:35,521
(I'm margarita.)

1937
01:09:35,621 --> 01:09:38,791
(Both new menu items have been ordered!)

1938
01:09:39,261 --> 01:09:41,090
Welcome.

1939
01:09:41,091 --> 01:09:43,560
Under whose name did you make the reservation?

1940
01:09:43,561 --> 01:09:44,930
- Are you here alone?
- Yes.

1941
01:09:44,931 --> 01:09:46,431
Okay. Nice to meet you.

1942
01:09:46,961 --> 01:09:49,930
- A beef burger and a carrot cake.
- Okay.

1943
01:09:49,931 --> 01:09:51,201
(Luckily, it's just 1 customer, so the order is simple.)

1944
01:09:51,541 --> 01:09:53,541
(She prepares the soda before she gets confused.)

1945
01:09:53,741 --> 01:09:55,540
I know you're busy, but please take a look at this.

1946
01:09:55,541 --> 01:09:56,640
This is the order it will be served.

1947
01:09:56,641 --> 01:09:58,540
- First, second, third.
- Okay.

1948
01:09:58,541 --> 01:10:00,411
- First, second, third.
- Okay.

1949
01:10:00,841 --> 01:10:04,381
(Young Ji places the beef patty on the grill...)

1950
01:10:04,721 --> 01:10:06,281
(and checks the tteokbokki.)

1951
01:10:06,481 --> 01:10:08,421
Are the fritters done, Mi Hyun?

1952
01:10:08,851 --> 01:10:10,521
They're done.

1953
01:10:12,561 --> 01:10:14,961
There's no need to rush.

1954
01:10:15,061 --> 01:10:17,601
(She hands them to the head chef.)

1955
01:10:17,901 --> 01:10:18,901
Thank you.

1956
01:10:19,301 --> 01:10:20,660
Can the original tteokbokki...

1957
01:10:20,661 --> 01:10:22,071
- be served first?
- Sure.

1958
01:10:23,201 --> 01:10:26,600
If it gets too tough in the kitchen, you can ask Yu Jin for help.

1959
01:10:26,601 --> 01:10:27,611
Okay.

1960
01:10:27,941 --> 01:10:29,211
- I'll work on the pizza.
- Okay.

1961
01:10:29,411 --> 01:10:32,281
(Since it's a new menu item, she carefully reads the recipe.)

1962
01:10:32,641 --> 01:10:35,251
(Yu Jin is in charge of pizza today.)

1963
01:10:35,811 --> 01:10:38,751
(She spreads the spicy sauce evenly,)

1964
01:10:39,181 --> 01:10:42,421
(sprinkles some mozzarella cheese,)

1965
01:10:42,851 --> 01:10:45,561
(adds chorizo,)

1966
01:10:45,921 --> 01:10:48,261
(adds button mushroom,)

1967
01:10:48,761 --> 01:10:51,501
(and bakes it in the oven.)

1968
01:10:51,961 --> 01:10:54,401
(While the pizza bakes,)

1969
01:10:55,001 --> 01:10:57,871
(Eun Ji is preparing another new menu item.)

1970
01:10:58,301 --> 01:11:01,171
(She adds the ingredients.)

1971
01:11:01,611 --> 01:11:04,171
(Shaking)

1972
01:11:04,481 --> 01:11:08,051
(Role satisfaction: 116 percent)

1973
01:11:08,411 --> 01:11:10,011
(Rimming the glass with lemon juice)

1974
01:11:10,311 --> 01:11:12,651
(Dipping it in sugar)

1975
01:11:13,151 --> 01:11:14,921
(She pours it into a glass.)

1976
01:11:15,551 --> 01:11:18,191
(Goheung sea margarita is ready.)

1977
01:11:18,761 --> 01:11:21,131
(Yu Jin gets out the cakes she prepared earlier...)

1978
01:11:21,591 --> 01:11:24,061
(and completes them with cute carrot cakes.)

1979
01:11:24,461 --> 01:11:26,331
It's 1, 2, and 3 from the left, right?

1980
01:11:26,501 --> 01:11:27,971
That's right.

1981
01:11:28,571 --> 01:11:30,971
It's too early for the carrot cake, but it's out first.

1982
01:11:32,001 --> 01:11:34,301
(The dessert orders are moving too fast.)

1983
01:11:34,611 --> 01:11:36,871
- Can the tteokbokki be served?
- Yes.

1984
01:11:37,741 --> 01:11:39,681
The shrimp burger will be ready soon.

1985
01:11:40,181 --> 01:11:42,311
(The tteokbokki is ready first.)

1986
01:11:42,681 --> 01:11:44,381
(Eun Ji is about to serve it.)

1987
01:11:44,681 --> 01:11:45,750
(Spilling)

1988
01:11:45,751 --> 01:11:49,120
Goodness. My margarita.

1989
01:11:49,121 --> 01:11:50,691
- What's wrong with you?
- Margarita?

1990
01:11:51,621 --> 01:11:54,331
- Okay.
- The margarita became like this.

1991
01:11:55,061 --> 01:11:57,860
Serving margaritas up the stairs will be hard.

1992
01:11:57,861 --> 01:11:58,861
(Worrying about the margaritas)

1993
01:11:58,862 --> 01:12:00,830
(Carrot cake for Table 1, carrot cake for Table 2)

1994
01:12:00,831 --> 01:12:02,971
How am I going to take the margarita up the stairs?

1995
01:12:03,671 --> 01:12:05,641
- It won't be easy.
- What should I do with it?

1996
01:12:05,741 --> 01:12:06,770
I should take it separately.

1997
01:12:06,771 --> 01:12:08,340
(She separates the margarita.)

1998
01:12:08,341 --> 01:12:09,541
It's not easy.

1999
01:12:10,211 --> 01:12:12,681
Isn't there a dumbwaiter for dishes?

2000
01:12:13,781 --> 01:12:15,981
(She serves the dishes without the margarita first.)

2001
01:12:16,351 --> 01:12:18,850
Young Ji's original tteokbokki is here.

2002
01:12:18,851 --> 01:12:19,951
Thank you.

2003
01:12:20,121 --> 01:12:21,520
I'll serve the cute carrot cake as well.

2004
01:12:21,521 --> 01:12:22,521
- Yes.
- Thank you.

2005
01:12:22,522 --> 01:12:23,890
- Did we order 2 carrot cakes?
- I ordered 1.

2006
01:12:23,891 --> 01:12:25,061
Did you order one carrot cake?

2007
01:12:26,021 --> 01:12:27,831
- Yes.
- Then I'll take one back.

